    "created_at": "2018-08-12T06:20:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-12T06:20:49Z",
    "body": "Right, OK.\r\n\r\n> That still seems like the correct tradeoff given the complexity (also consider the API side, impact on Selectors, etc.).\r\n\r\nOK, I wasn't aware of the API and Selectors issues. Perhaps that needs to be added to one of the two FAQs.\r\n\r\n> Yeah, I consider this answered by the FAQ\r\n\r\nI knew from way back that the old FAQ mentioned this issue, but I looked for it but could not find that old FAQ. I therefore didn't think the FAQ was up anymore and assumed the WHATWG was just using the new FAQ as there is no link to the old one from the whatwg.org home page. I found this -> https://whatwg.org/faq but could not see the href=\"\" addressed there. Perhaps there needs to be a link to the other FAQ from the WHATWG homepage, or the bottom of the FAQ that is linked to from the home page? I'll leave it to you guys to decide if there needs to be any changes made to the FAQ pages. I trust your / the browser-vendor's judgement that the proposal can not be implemented.\r\n\r\nThanks\r\n",
